      "message": "@bungeman, would you like to take a look as a Skia TL?  Note that @kjlubick is already reviewing this CL (thanks!), but this is the first encoding-related CL, so I thought that it would be nice to give Skia TLs a chance to take a quick look.  (At any rate, I\u0027ll ask @fmalita to review the follow-up, more meaty CLs, so we can always iterate and/or change things in the future if needed.)\n\nI hope that this CL is non-controversial:\n\n* The `SkPngRustEncoder.h` API mimics the subset of `SkPngEncoder.h` APIs (only 2 functions + not taking `Options` for now - until https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/924461 and https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/924544)\n* The `SkPngRustEncoder.cc` mostly duplicates bits of `SkPngEncoder.cpp`.  It seems to me that this level of duplication is okay.\n* The `SkPngRustEncoderImpl.h/.cc` are mostly stubs, so probably not that important to get right on the first try.  The follow-up CLs evolve those (e.g. see https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/923337).\n* This is all under `experimental/` so it will only used from Chromium in the short-term (behind `enable_rust_png` GN arg, behind `base::Feature`), although Chromium won\u0027t actually use this until https://crrev.com/c/6044082 (which itself depends on a few extra Skia-side CLs).\n\nSome other background notes:\n\n* I am a Chrome Security engineer working on `SkPngRustCodec` - see https://docs.google.com/document/d/1glx5ue5JDlCld5WzWgTOGK3wsMErQFnkY5N5Dsbi91Y/edit?usp\u003dsharing for more details about this project.\n* @fmalita (in CC) is a Skia TL that I usually work with, but they suggested that around Thanksgiving I may work with you instead.",
